hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19151","Waki narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Najiya al-Khuzai, he said, keeper of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I said: How shall I do with what is injured of the sacrificial camels? He said: Slaughter it, dip its sandal in its blood, strike its flank, and leave between the people and it to eat it."
"19152","Abu Muawiya narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Najiya al-Khuzai, keeper of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall I do with what is injured of the camels or sacrificial camels? He said: Slaughter it, then cast its sandal in its blood, then leave it and the people to eat it."
